<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pagondas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 424 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pagondas was a Theban commander and Boeotarch who led the Boeotian army to victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-delium">Battle of Delium</a> in 424 BCE. He persuaded his reluctant fellow commanders to fight, drew up the Thebans 25 ranks deep and sent cavalry round a hill to surprise the Athenian flank. His tactics are often seen as an early example of the deep formations later used by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epaminondas">Epaminondas</a>.</p></div>
